# Design Work (Canva + Claude MCP)

When the user asks for **design work** - brand assets, social graphics, presentations, decks, marketing creatives, Canva layouts, or visual design production - use the **Canva** and **Claude** MCP servers. Do not invent standalone mockups or skip these tools when Canva can produce the asset.

## Workflow

1. Discover tools with `GetMcpTools` on `canva` and `claude` (or pattern `canva|claude`).
2. Prefer **Canva** (`https://mcp.canva.com/mcp`) to create, search, edit, autofill, comment on, and export designs.
3. Use **Claude** (`https://code.claude.com/docs/mcp`) for Claude Code / Anthropic documentation and guidance when design automation or tooling needs it.
4. If Canva tools fail with auth errors, tell the user to open Settings → Tools & MCP and **Connect** Canva, then retry.

## Scope vs NanoGPT images

- **Canva**: editable designs, brand kit, templates, exports (PDF, PNG, etc.).
- **NanoGPT** (see `nanogpt-images.mdc`): one-off AI raster image generation when the user wants generated pixels, not a Canva design.
